---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { getGitDates, formatDate } from '../../lib/git-dates';

// Section hub, added when nicotine pouches got their own section
// (2026-10-02) — previously one subsection of /india/law/. Links down to
// /nicotine-pouches/legal-status/ (moved from /india/nicotine-pouches/)
// and the new /nicotine-pouches/safety/.
const pageDates = getGitDates('src/pages/nicotine-pouches/index.astro');

const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Nicotine Pouches in India: Legal Status and Safety',
  datePublished: pageDates.published,
  dateModified: pageDates.modified,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Association of Vapers India' },
};
---
<Base
  title="Nicotine Pouches in India: Legal Status and Safety"
  rawTitle={true}
  description="What nicotine pouches are, why there's no legal way to sell one in India as of September 2026, how their risk compares with smoking or gutka, and what AVI wants to see change."
  image="/og/india-law.png"
  wide={true}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleLd)} />

  <section class="breakout pouch-hub-hero">
    <div class="breakout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Updated {formatDate(pageDates.modified)}</p>
      <h1>Nicotine pouches in India</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pouch-hub-body">
    <p class="intro">
      Nicotine pouches sit under the lip. They contain nicotine but no
      tobacco leaf, and nothing is burned. Sweden, where similar products
      are widely used, has the lowest smoking rate in Europe at about 5
      percent. In India no law bans them, but since September 2026 there
      is no legal way to sell them.
    </p>

    <div class="hub-cards">
      <a href="/nicotine-pouches/legal-status/" class="hub-card">
        <Icon name="document" />
        <h2>Legal status</h2>
        <p>No law names them, but a two-agency regulatory freeze closed every lawful route to sell one.</p>
        <span class="hub-cta">Read the legal status →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/nicotine-pouches/safety/" class="hub-card">
        <Icon name="heart" />
        <h2>Safety</h2>
        <p>How their risk compares with smoking and with gutka or khaini — and what the FDA's own review found.</p>
        <span class="hub-cta">Read the evidence →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#what-avi-wants" class="hub-card">
        <Icon name="megaphone" />
        <h2>What AVI wants</h2>
        <p>Regulation, not a freeze — while a far more dangerous product stays legal at every paan shop.</p>
        <span class="hub-cta">Read AVI's position →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="what-avi-wants"><Icon name="megaphone" /> What AVI wants</h2>
    <p class="wants-text">
      Regulate pouches as lower-risk products, with quality standards,
      honest labels and sale to adults only. Don't freeze them out while
      gutka and khaini are sold at every paan shop.
    </p>

    <div class="hub-related">
      <a href="/india/smokeless-tobacco/" class="related-card">
        <h3>India's smokeless tobacco users →</h3>
        <p>The harm reduction case for the roughly 200 million Indians who use gutka, khaini or other SLT.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/india/law/" class="related-card">
        <h3>Vaping law, in full →</h3>
        <p>What PECA bans for e-cigarettes, for contrast.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--paper);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .pouch-hub-hero {
      background: var(--green-deep);
      padding: 3.25rem 0 2.75rem;
    }
    .pouch-hub-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.6rem); }

    .pouch-hub-body { max-width: var(--max-w-wide); margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.75rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
    .intro { max-width: var(--max-w); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; }

    .hub-cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(15.5rem, 100%), 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin: 0 0 3rem;
    }
    .hub-card {
      display: block;
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.6rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .hub-card:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .hub-card :global(svg) { width: 1.8rem; height: 1.8rem; color: var(--green); margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
    .hub-card h2 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    .hub-card p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .hub-cta { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--green-deep); }

    h2 {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      max-width: var(--max-w);
    }
    h2 :global(svg) { width: 1.3rem; height: 1.3rem; color: var(--green); flex-shrink: 0; }
    .wants-text { max-width: var(--max-w); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 3rem; }

    .hub-related {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(15rem, 100%), 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .related-card {
      display: block;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
      background: var(--paper-2);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .related-card:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .related-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--green-deep); }
    .related-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  </style>
</Base>
